# Code ownership for canary
#
# This is a solo-developer repository, so every path resolves to a single
# owner (@heznpc). CODEOWNERS still earns its keep here because it:
#   1. Makes the paper-side / service-side / governance-side split that
#      CLAUDE.md describes explicit and enforceable by branch-protection
#      "Require review from Code Owners" — a future external contributor
#      gets routed for review just like an internal change would.
#   2. Pairs with the §5.4 push-leakage thesis: when ownership is encoded
#      in a file the operator does not have to remember, ownership-related
#      mistakes (cross-bounded-context accidental merges) become invisible
#      to the operator in the same way push-leakage does — surfacing them
#      via tooling is the fix.
#
# Order matters: later patterns override earlier ones.

# Default owner — fallback for any path not matched below.
*                       @heznpc

# Research / paper-side bounded contexts (CLAUDE.md "paper edit and a code
# edit, never just one").
/paper/                 @heznpc
/experiments/           @heznpc
/literature/            @heznpc
/planning/              @heznpc
/submissions/           @heznpc
/CITATION.cff           @heznpc
/.zenodo.json           @heznpc

# Service-side bounded contexts.
/app/                   @heznpc
/components/            @heznpc
/lib/                   @heznpc
/mcp/                   @heznpc
/public/                @heznpc
/scripts/               @heznpc
